* Aztec
** Two execution\nenvironments
*** PXE\nclient-side, proves\nprivate functions
*** AVM\nsequencer-side,\npublic functions
*** Private runs first,\npublic is enqueued
*** Utility functions\nunconstrained, offchain
** State model
*** Notes\nUTXO commitments in\nthe note hash tree
*** Nullifiers\nspend without\nrevealing the note
*** Public data tree\nsparse, EVM-like
*** Slots siloed by\ncontract address
** Keys
*** Nullifier keys\nspend, app-siloed
*** Incoming viewing key\ndecrypt received notes
*** Signing key\nchosen by the\naccount contract
*** Reserved slots\novpk, tpk, mspk, fbpk
** Note delivery
*** offchain\nno cost, no guarantee
*** onchain_unconstrained\nDA cost, sender trusted
*** onchain_constrained\nDA + proving,\nguaranteed
*** Tagging\nposeidon2(secret, index)
** Transaction\nlifecycle
*** Kernel circuits\ninit, inner, reset,\ntail
*** ~290k gates fixed\n~101k per extra call
*** Rollup circuits\ntx, block, checkpoint,\nepoch
*** Epoch proof\nverified on L1
** Fees
*** Mana\nDA and L2 dimensions
*** Fee Juice\nbridged, non-transferable
*** EIP-1559 style\ncongestion multiplier
** Portals
*** L1 to L2 inbox
*** L2 to L1 outbox
*** Pull, not push\nkeeps args private
** What still leaks
*** enqueue reveals\nmsg_sender
*** Public call arguments\nare public
*** Counts of public calls\nand L2 to L1 messages
*** Node queries reveal\nwhat you read
@endmindmap
